    "adaptations": "Foundation: No defender, walking, larger square, soft ball.\nIntermediate: Shadow defender at 50%, three-second hold.\nAdvanced: Defender up to 75%, two-second hold, moving reception.\nLarge group: Six small squares and rotating observer; no queues.\nSmall group: 3v2 or triangle with one defender.\nLimited space: 4×4 squares, walking, short passes.\nLimited equipment: One ball per four; parallel no-ball movement task.\nDifferent needs: Strong visual marks, one instruction at a time, fixed partner, closer support points, or approved individual plan.",
    "assessment": "Checks: Response time, angle, hand target, spacing, communication.\nSuccess: Four of five criteria in six of eight sequences.\nPartial success: Three criteria or reliable performance only without a defender.\nNot yet successful: Remains stationary, creates collision risk, or cannot offer a lane after prompting.\nResponse: Return to the unopposed triangle or two-cone walking rehearsal.",
    "reflection": "Teacher: Was activity time high? Were squares suitable? Who needed a cue? Was defender intensity safe?\nStudents: How did you choose where to move? What helped the passer see you? When did movement close space?\nNext improvement: Adjust area size and identify who is ready for pass-or-dribble decisions.",
    "continuity": "If achieved: Basketball 06—receive on the move and decide pass or dribble.\nIf not achieved: Repeat “pass and fill” without a defender; return to Basketball 03 if pass/catch accuracy is the barrier.",
